#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build explicit metadata for the composition and endpoint-model assertions."""
from pathlib import Path
import json

rows = [
('C.1','The raw all-type path categories form a strictly unital associative Cat-enrichment; their nerves and product-preserving Kan replacements give a simplicial category and a Segal model.','Proved','B.1','IX-037','No mapping-space comparison is required for the raw enrichment.'),
('C.2','Weak-vertical hammocks give a composition-compatible model of simplicial localization; this theorem alone does not replace arbitrary vertical arrows.','Known','B.2','IX-037','Dwyer–Kan Definition 2.1 and Propositions 3.1, 3.3; exact all-type comparison in B.2.'),
('C.3','Pointed Cartesian composition cannot give the intended zero-preserving units unless identities equal zero; smash composition has the correct unit S0.','Proved','','IX-044; IX-049','The correction at IX ms.17 is verified with its exact unit.'),
('C.4','Cofibrant-fibrant objects in a pointed simplicial model category supply Kan mapping spaces with strict absorbing zero, smash composition, and S0-units.','Proved','C.3; B.2','IX-044; IX-049; IX-052','A sufficient modern setting; transfer to literal pointed stabilized paths is not silently inferred.'),
('C.5','Quillen’s fundamental groupoid agrees naturally with that of the derived mapping complex under cofibrant/fibrant replacement; specified vertices and basepoint paths determine the corresponding pi1 comparisons.','Known','B.2','IX-040; IX-041; IX-072','For the literal full path category the comparison retains B.8 and pointed compatibility.'),
('C.6','Pointed infinity categories with the required pullbacks and pushouts have mapping-space loop/suspension formulas; a pointed derivator has the corresponding adjunction and exact morphisms.','Proved','','IX-084; IX-087','The hypotheses include enhanced homotopy limits and colimits; mere pi1-representability is insufficient.'),
('C.7','Representability of all pi1 mapping functors does not imply the mapping-space loop formulas.','Refuted','','IX-084; tests (a) and (c)','Full pointed infinity subcategory on *, S0 and K(Z,2); zero functors represent pi1 while the K(Z,1) loop space is noncontractible.'),
('C.8','For complexes of modules over a commutative ring k, truncated derived Hom takes values in D^{<=0}(k), with derived-tensor composition, units, and the prescribed mapping-space homotopy groups.','Proved','C.6','IX-061; IX-065; IX-070','Fixed dg-projective replacements; good truncation; Koszul signs; a=k,b=k[1] gives K(k,1).'),
('C.9','The general additive relative-category proposal has not been proved from the manuscript’s unspecified additional axioms, or merely from finite-sum closure of a saturated weak class.','Open','C.8; B.8','IX-061; IX-065; IX-070','Dugger–Shipley’s stronger additive-resolution hypotheses are retained; no general dg-refinement theorem is claimed.'),
('C.10','The literal pointed and pointed-ind-category refinements of stabilized full paths remain unresolved in the stated generality.','Open','C.3; C.4; C.P5; B.8','IX-044; IX-049; IX-052; IX-072','Exact missing conditions are absorbing zero coherences and compatibility with specified comparisons.'),
('E.1','The checked CATHOT all-arrows theorem identifies exact endpoint fibres with path spaces, even translation with identity in Hot, and the one-sided constant-tail maps as weak equivalences.','Known','C.P3; C.P4','CATHOT E.20-E.25; VIIc-C004; VIIc-C005','Supplied proofs independently checked; all-arrows proof cited without being redone; shorter qL proof verified.'),
('E.2','The all-type categorical loop model is strictly monoidal, natural in pointed functors, and realizes the loop space with its A-infinity multiplication.','Proved','E.1; B.2; C.1','Part E; IX-037','Uses products and concatenation, without pushout-product axioms or fibrant replacement of X.'),
('E.3','The all-type endpoint functor is smooth but can fail properness and both strict Grothendieck lifting properties, already for X=[1].','Refuted','E.1','VII ms.161-166; Part E; STRATA path test','Empty-type outgoing lift is empty; every proposed incoming terminal path receives two distinct reparametrized maps.'),
('E.4','The eventual alternating endpoint functor is smooth and proper but need not be a Grothendieck fibration or opfibration.','Refuted','E.1','Part E; filtered-union lifting distinction','Delayed-transition paths in [1] rule out terminal and initial lifts; finite-support truncations cannot settle this.'),
('E.5','Every functor has a natural categorical mapping-path factorization into a nerve weak equivalence followed by a smooth proper functor whose strict fibres are homotopy fibres.','Proved','E.1; E.4','Part E; XII ms.188-207','Actual functors and base-change argument specified; no claim of a Thomason model factorization.'),
('E.6','For the five-element rectangular-band monoid of type S2, the eventual path endpoint map is neither a strict fibration nor opfibration; the all-type map is not an opfibration.','Refuted','E.3; E.4','STRATA E.11 test case','All 125 associativity equations and delayed-transition naturality equations checked; does not refute another bifibration model.'),
('E.7','For every n>=1 the specified interval pushout-product is a weak equivalence but not an intrinsic W_infinity-cofibration.','Refuted','','POLES H.6; TOTASPH F.23; Part E','Explicit sieve pushout changes a contractible source into S3; n=1,2,3 complete tables and rational homology checked.'),
('E.8','Finite interval cotensors have a constant-section categorical homotopy equivalence but their exact endpoint fibres need not be the correct path spaces.','Proved','','Part E; dual interval assertion','X=[1], interval=[1], endpoints (1,0) give empty strict fibre while the topological path space is contractible.'),
('E.9','W_infinity smoothness/properness does not imply universal preservation under strict pullback for a larger localizer.','Refuted','E.1','GALOIS/STRATA localizer qualification; Part E','For B C2, rational homology equivalence point→B C2 pulls back to a map with H0 Q^2→Q.'),
('E.10','Components of the marked subcategory alone do not specify a stratification whose exit paths compute general localization mapping spaces.','Refuted','B.4','STRATA proposed general stratified reading','One-object monoid {1,e},e^2=e, with identity marking: contractible classifying space but a two-point endomorphism space.'),
('E.11','Existence of another strict bifibration realizing the path local system over the rectangular-band monoid remains unresolved here.','Open','E.6','STRATA E.11; VIc-C022','Standard path models fail; their failure is not a proof that no replacement exists.'),
('E.12','The checked fixed-origin all-type path category may be contractible without being filtered or totally aspherical; its endpoint functor is final over simply connected bases.','Known','E.1','TOTASPH G.1-G.6; XIIba-C005','Finite fork and the explicit four-object sphere category give the verified separation.'),
('E.13','Finite set-valued restricted Yoneda on finite-category test objects is not faithful: the finitary symmetric-group shift and the identity induce the same tests but are distinct in Hot.','Refuted','','VIIc-C004 faithfulness question; CATHOT F.2 verification','Actual endofunctor of an infinite one-object category; the proof handles every finite-category test. The equality T^2=1 is independently proved in E.1.'),
]
root = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
out=[]
for ident,statement,status,depends,pages,notes in rows:
    section = 'sections/C.tex' if ident.startswith('C.') else 'sections/E.tex'
    out.append(dict(id=ident,statement=statement,status=status,where_proved=f'{section}, {ident}',
                    depends_on=depends,manuscript_rows_or_pages_settled=pages,notes=notes))
(root/'research/CE_results.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print(f'Wrote {len(out)} rows.')
print({s:sum(r['status']==s for r in out) for s in ['Proved','Refuted','Known','Open']})
